</given-names></name><name><surname>Rieul</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Duclos</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Cozzone</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of the phosphoproteins of <italic>Escherichia coli </italic>cells by electrophoretic analysis</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><year>1986</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3530754</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Trojanek</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Klimecka</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fraser</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dobrowolska</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Muszynska</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of dual specificity protein kinase from maize seedlings</article-title><source>Acta Biochim Pol</source><year>2004</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>635</fpage><lpage>647</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15448726</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirayama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Oka</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Novel protein kinase of <italic>Arabidopsis thaliana </italic>(APK1) that phosphorylates tyrosine, serine and threonine</article-title><source>Plant Mol Biol</source><year>1992</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>653</fpage><lpage>662</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1450380</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Esch</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phosphorylation sites in enolase and lactate dehydrogenase utilized by tyrosine protein kinases in vivo and in vitro</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1984</year><volume>259</volume><fpage>7835</fpage><lpage>7841</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6330085</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reiss</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Three glycolytic enzymes are phosphorylated at tyrosine in cells transformed by Rous sarcoma virus</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1983</year><volume>302</volume><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6188054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gorlich</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kutay</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transport between the cell nucleus and the cytoplasm</article-title><source>Annu Rev Cell Dev Biol</source><year>1999</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>660</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10611974</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>